From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:20:48 -0400
Subject: spaces: isolate cookies per Space in a storage partition

An optional Independent session on a Space puts its new tabs in a
non-default StoragePartition so the same site can be signed into
twice in one window. Off, Spaces share the profile jar as today.
Extensions, settings, history and saved passwords stay on the
profile (ADR 0019).

Why: docs/features/sessions.md S1-S7, ADR 0019.
Removable when: Chromium offers per-tab storage partitions as a
product feature, or Spaces become full Profiles.
